./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:3:The current matcher confuses two catalog-relevant control states: a valve supplied with an electric actuator and a valve only prepared for a future actuator. Public results show that the reranker can select an underground or actuator-ready variant when the tender requests an ordinary electrically actuated variant (and vice versa), even though the catalog represents these states with distinct terms. Earlier selection and prompt interventions were neutral or regressive; a bounded retrieval-only representation is the remaining evidence-backed, low-risk experiment.
