./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:8:- Distinguish explicit installed-electric wording (for example, `с электроприводом`) from explicit actuator-ready wording (for example, `под электропривод`) and expand each only with its corresponding catalog-native vocabulary.
./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:11:- Reuse the existing original-plus-one-alternate hybrid retrieval, per-modality deduplication, RRF, limits, and alternate-query fail-open behavior.
./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:17:- `retrieval-actuation-intent-canonicalization`: Generates a safe, state-specific alternate retrieval representation for explicit electric-actuation tender language.
./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:25:- Affected package code: `query_canonicalization.py` and focused canonicalization tests; the established matcher and hybrid-retriever alternate-query interfaces are reused unchanged.
./openspec/changes/cycle-14-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md:26:- Affected behavior: only hybrid candidate generation for explicitly stated installed-electric or actuator-ready intent may gain one catalog-native alternate query.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:16:- **THEN** the system performs candidate generation with the original normalized text and does not manufacture an alternate query
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:19:The system SHALL deterministically normalize only supported lexical forms: mixed-script confusables within designation-like tokens, compact DN/PN notation, quantity/noise suffixes, and documented joining or actuation abbreviations. It SHALL preserve explicit product, DN, PN, material, joining, control, and designation requirements and SHALL NOT infer an unmentioned engineering property or a catalog product identifier.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:23:- **THEN** the alternate retrieval representation contains the normalized token and preserves its surrounding item constraints
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:26:- **WHEN** a tender item uses a supported compact joining or actuation notation
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:27:- **THEN** the alternate representation contains catalog-native lexical equivalents without adding DN, PN, material, special execution, or product-family requirements absent from the tender
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/specs/retrieval-query-canonicalization/spec.md:31:- **THEN** the alternate representation retains the item clause and its nearby technical attributes while omitting only non-nomenclature noise
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:11:- Make alternate retrieval text inspectable and deterministic so it can be unit-tested and removed cleanly if the experiment is rejected.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:25:Introduce a small pure query-canonicalization boundary returning the normalized original and either zero or one canonical retrieval query. It will apply a narrowly documented table/rule set: confusable-character repair only for alphanumeric designation tokens, standard spacing for compact DN/PN forms, supported joining/actuation abbreviations, removal of count-only suffixes, and extraction of a supported item clause from surrounding prose when it is unambiguous.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:37:The reranker continues to receive the original normalized tender string, not the alternate representation. Candidate objects keep the current retrieval evidence contract; the canonicalization result should be available in an optional, non-production diagnostic path suitable for tests and local debugging. If alternate-query retrieval raises an operational error, the original-query retrieval result remains usable rather than failing the whole match.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:44:- [An extracted clause omits a necessary constraint] → Use clause extraction only when a supported product phrase anchors it; otherwise emit no alternate query and retain original retrieval.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:45:- [Additional retrieval calls increase latency] → At most one alternate query per unique non-blank request, reuse existing configured limits, and skip it when identical to the original.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:52:2. Integrate additive retrieval in the hybrid retriever while preserving its current API for callers without an alternate query.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/design.md:53:3. Wire the matcher to generate and pass at most one alternate retrieval representation while preserving result query text and caching semantics.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/tasks.md:3:- [x] 1.1 Add a small pure query-canonicalization module that returns a normalized source query and at most one distinct canonical retrieval query, covering only the documented confusable designation tokens, compact DN/PN forms, allowed joining/actuation abbreviations, count-only noise, and safely anchored item clauses; verify focused unit tests cover each supported transform and an unchanged-input no-op.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/tasks.md:5:- [x] 1.3 Ensure unsupported product wording, blank input, ambiguous/no-anchor prose, and already canonical text produce no catalog-domain expansion; verify focused negative and no-op tests.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/tasks.md:9:- [x] 2.1 Extend hybrid retrieval to accept an optional distinct canonical query and retrieve it in addition to the original query without changing the existing one-query caller behavior; verify mocked dense and BM25 tests assert both calls only when an alternate exists.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/tasks.md:11:- [x] 2.3 Preserve existing candidate payload fields, configured limits, and failure behavior when alternate retrieval is absent or fails; verify focused tests assert no duplicate candidates and usable original-query candidates after an alternate-query failure.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/proposal.md:8:- Normalize safe lexical variants that do not add engineering requirements: Unicode-confusable Latin/Cyrillic characters inside designation-like tokens, compact DN/PN notation, and known joining/actuation abbreviations.
./openspec/changes/cycle-03-query-canonicalization/proposal.md:11:- Keep negative, blank, and unsupported product queries from gaining catalog-domain expansion; retain present behavior if canonicalization produces no meaningful alternate query.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:3:Provide conservative, observable expansion of technical connection notation so terse tender requests can retrieve catalog candidates without changing their original decision semantics.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:23:The system SHALL NOT expand a connection code that is embedded in a larger alphanumeric token, is not on the approved unambiguous allowlist, or occurs in an unsupported/no-product query. When no other safe canonicalization applies, it SHALL produce no alternate retrieval query.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:33:- **THEN** the system produces no catalog-domain connection expansion
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:35:### Requirement: Keep alternate retrieval bounded and fail-open
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:37:The system SHALL use the alternate representation only as an additional retrieval input, at most once per query, and SHALL retain usable original-query retrieval candidates if alternate retrieval is unavailable or errors. It SHALL not duplicate a candidate solely because it was retrieved through both representations.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/specs/connection-notation-canonicalization/spec.md:41:- **WHEN** retrieval of the alternate representation fails after original-query retrieval succeeds
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/design.md:10:- Maintain a single alternate query and current original-query fail-open behavior.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/design.md:16:- No expansion of ambiguous codes such as `FF`/`MF`, whose meanings depend on product and thread context.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/design.md:29:Continue querying original text regardless of whether notation expansion produces an alternate. The pre-existing per-modality deduplication/RRF behavior applies without change, and reranking receives the source tender text. This isolates the experiment to candidate recall and preserves the outcome semantics that were safe in Cycle 3.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/design.md:31:Changing candidate score fusion or using canonical text as the reranker input is rejected because either would confound the effect of notation expansion and revisit the selection-adjacent risks observed in Cycles 1 and 2.
./openspec/changes/cycle-04-connection-notation-canonicalization/design.md:37:- [The extra query adds latency] → Reuse Cycle 3's at-most-one-alternate path and emit none when the representation would be unchanged.
